A thread that joins a queue is not linked from the newest waiter before it.
A signal would never reach it, and the ring would not close;
a notification's waiters are a ring linked both ways.

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -29,3 +29,3 @@
         t->wait_prev = oldest->wait_prev;
-        newest->wait_next = self;
+        (void)newest;
         oldest->wait_prev = self;
